cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "chinese-de-ai-writing: evidence-graded de-AI editing skill for Simplified Chinese"
message: "If you use this skill or its validation results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tang"
    given-names: "Wenwen"
    affiliation: "Department of Pediatric Neurosurgery, Affiliated Women and Children's Hospital of Ningbo University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tangwenwen-md/chinese-de-ai-writing"
abstract: >
  An agent skill (Claude Code / Agent Skills format) for auditing and editing
  AI-sounding patterns in Simplified Chinese text. Rules are graded by evidence:
  only features that hold up in human/AI corpus comparisons are enforced;
  popular but refuted rules are listed as things not to do. The top constraint
  is information conservation: no invented facts, cases, numbers or quotes, and
  no change to claim strength. Includes a regex scanner with human/AI baselines
  and a reproducible validation against HC3-Chinese and Claude-generated text.
keywords:
  - Chinese
  - AI-generated text
  - writing
  - agent skill
  - Claude Code
  - medical communication
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
